<section aria-labelledby="demo-h">
  <h2 id="demo-h" class="type-h2">Credits</h2>
  <p>Credits is the only yellow band on a case study. The jump nav uses yellow only for its current link. Every case study gets one when other roles contributed to the work. A solo project gets none. It sits under the <a href="/components/outcome/">Outcome</a> and above the <a href="/components/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>. It lists roles, one per line, written as "Role: phrase." It uses the same two-column row as the <a href="/components/section-split/">Section split</a>. The text below is placeholder text.</p>
  {% demo "Credits with placeholder roles", "block" %}
  <section class="cs-credits" aria-labelledby="credits-demo-h">
    <div class="cs-row">
      <h3 class="cs-credits__heading type-h2" id="credits-demo-h">Credits</h3>
      <ul class="cs-credits__list type-body" role="list">
        <li>Product manager: set the goals and the order of the work.</li>
        <li>Engineers: built the designs and shipped them.</li>
        <li>Researcher: ran the interviews and shared what they heard.</li>
        <li>Content designer: wrote and edited the words on screen.</li>
        <li>Data analyst: measured what changed after launch.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="layout-h">
  <h2 id="layout-h" class="type-h2">Layout and spacing</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Credits spacing by breakpoint, scrollable">
    <table class="docs-table type-small">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Breakpoint</th><th scope="col">Padding above and below</th><th scope="col">Gap between heading and list</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Mobile</th><td>40px</td><td>24px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tablet (768px up)</th><td>48px</td><td>32px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Desktop (1024px up)</th><td>64px</td><td>The heading takes columns 1 to 8, the list columns 9 to 12</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The side padding is the page padding. Roles in the list are 16px apart, which reads as the blank line between paragraphs.</p>
  <h3 class="type-h3">How much fits</h3>
  <p>The list holds up to 60 words and 400 characters. Count the blank lines between roles as characters. The example above is 5 roles, 43 words and 273 characters, counting the four blank lines. If a list is longer, cut the phrases before you cut a role.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="color-h">
  <h2 id="color-h" class="type-h2">Color</h2>
  <p>The band is <code>surface/brand/secondary-band</code>. The heading is <code>text/on-secondary/primary</code> and the list is <code>text/on-secondary/body</code>. The text is near-black on yellow in both Light and Dark.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the credits</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Write one role per line as "Role: phrase." and say what the role did.</li>
      <li>List roles, not names.</li>
      <li>Leave the band out on a solo project.</li>
      <li>Use <code>border/focus/ring-on-secondary</code> for any link on the band. A white ring fails on yellow.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Use the yellow band for anything other than credits.</li>
      <li>Name a person, a client or an employer. Roles only.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="a11y-h">
  <h2 id="a11y-h" class="type-h2">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The band is a <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> named by its <code>h2</code>. The list is a real list.</li>
    <li>The text is near-black on yellow in both Light and Dark.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
